      "value": "@{6362bc2c0c1fc355a4c3dd2d|full_name}: I think the other controllers you've been using play animations depending on what buttons you're touching/pressing? In which case, fully extending thumbs is entirely down to the animations on the avatar itself. Since you get finger tracking with Index controllers, avatars won't play any animations on the fingers by default unless the avatar is set up to allow for toggling whether fingers use animations or tracking using an \"Animator Tracking Control\" state behaviour.\n\nIf you want to increase thumb extension on your avatar on index controllers, you can adjust the maximum movement of the thumb muscles in the humanoid rig in Unity. Adjusting the position of the thumb in the T-Pose in the humanoid rig will also give different results. Though note that making these changes to the humanoid rig/muscles will also affect the other thumb's movement on index when you touch the control stick/face buttons and will affect the movement of any humanoid finger animations. If the avatar might be used by someone not using index controllers, you may want to set custom hand gesture animations or at least make sure the default ones don't look too bad.\n\nAn old guide on adjusting thumbs by changing their position in the t-pose: https://voxelloop.co.uk/vrc/fix.html\n\nIf it's not your avatar that you want to adjust the thumbs of then I think you're out of luck.\n\nThere's a bunch of information in Tupper's comments on this canny post: https://vrchat.canny.io/feature-requests/p/785-add-script-to-allow-setting-minmax-muscle-values-used-for-index-tracking\n\nWhile it's a bit old now, most of the information is still probably relevant.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    }
  ],
  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2022-11-29T10:24:39.192Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "I've been using Pico/Oculus-style controllers for a while and just got to test drive my Index.\nI cannot extend my thumbs completely when using the Index controllers. I also see this with friends that have an Index.\nThumb movement tracks fine but when I completely lift my thumb the thumb on my avatar stops at like 30° rather than going to full 90°.",
